  "full_response": "No, not all rich people are corrupt. Wealth and corruption are not inherently linked. Many wealthy individuals have earned their fortunes through hard work, innovation, creativity, and ethical business practices. Some rich people are also known for their philanthropy, donating significant portions of their wealth to charitable causes, education, healthcare, and social initiatives.\n\nHowever, wealth can sometimes provide opportunities or temptations that may lead to unethical behavior, such as exploiting power, avoiding taxes, or engaging in fraud. Corruption is a complex issue influenced by factors like personal values, societal norms, legal systems, and economic pressures—not just wealth.\n\nIt’s important to judge individuals based on their actions and character rather than making broad assumptions about entire groups. Many rich people contribute positively to society, while others may engage in unethical or illegal behavior—just like people from any economic background.",
